@flexiarg argument-coherence/claims-as-hypotheses
@title State the Contribution as Hypotheses
@keywords hypotheses, principles, testable claims, outcome measures
@audience paper and proposal authors, reviewers, who-benefits analysts
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Mined from the Peeragogy "Greatest Flops" archive (~/notes/peeragogy-flops): the three LAK 2011 reviews of flop 1 (appendices/01, 'Reviews'); Joe's five-question analysis of flop 1 in the outtakes (appendices/07). Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29.
@status draft 2026-10-29; to test blind on the other flops, with Corneli 2016 (ICCC) and the Peeragogy Handbook as controls that should pass
@references [argument-coherence/ARGUMENT argument-coherence/evidence-the-venue-counts argument-coherence/earn-the-coined-term argument-coherence/one-worked-instance argument-coherence/say-how-it-carries-back argument-coherence/show-the-deliverable argument-coherence/plan-at-reviewable-grain]

! conclusion:
  State the contribution as claims a reader could check, each with the outcome that would count for or against it, rather than as principles.

  + context:
    Principles describe a stance; hypotheses can be tested. Early theory tends to stay at principles.

  + IF:
    The argument puts forward a theory or approach.

  + HOWEVER:
    Not every claim can be operationalised yet; forcing measures onto early ideas can make them look worse than they are.

  + THEN:
    Turn each central principle into at least one hypothesis with the observation that would support or count against it, and say which ones are not yet testable.

  + BECAUSE:
    Review 1 of flop 1: 'the desired outcome/performance measures did not appear much in the discussion'. Joe's analysis names the gain: 'the bullet points above are a set of hypotheses, whereas before we only had principles. This is a considerable step forward for our thinking.'

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Test blind: a reviewer given only a flop and this family; compare its rows with the recorded verdicts.]
